      "body": "## Motivation\n\nSGLang ignores `use_rslora` in a PEFT adapter config. PEFT scales an rsLoRA adapter by `lora_alpha / sqrt(r)` ([Kalajdzievski 2023](https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.03732)), but `LoRAAdapter` always uses `lora_alpha / r`.\n\nThe adapter loads without error, and its update is `sqrt(r)` times too weak: 4x at r=16, 8x at r=64.\n\n```\nuse_rslora=True:  PEFT scaling=16.0,  SGLang scaling=2.0   # wrong\nuse_rslora=False: PEFT scaling=2.0,   SGLang scaling=2.0   # correct\n```\n\nReported in #40835 with a full reproduction script.\n\n## Modifications\n\n**`python/sglang/srt/lora/lora_config.py`**\n- Parse `use_rslora` from the PEFT adapter config (defaults to `False`).\n\n**`python/sglang/srt/lora/lora.py`**\n- When `use_rslora` is `True`, compute `scaling = lora_alpha / sqrt(r)` instead of `lora_alpha / r`.\n\n**`test/registered/lora/test_rslora_scaling.py`** (new, 64 lines)\n- Parametrized unit tests across three (r, alpha) pairs verifying:\n  - Standard LoRA scaling matches `alpha / r`\n  - rsLoRA scaling matches `alpha / sqrt(r)`\n  - rsLoRA scaling is strictly larger than standard for any r > 1\n- Separate test confirming `use_rslora` defaults to `False` when absent from the config dict.\n\n## Checklist\n- [x] Format: `pre-commit run --all-files` passed.\n- [x] Test: unit test added covering both code paths and the default.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41808159481](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41808159481)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41808159339](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41808159339)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41808159177](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41808159177)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
